<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shiva</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shiva is one of the principal gods of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hinduism</a>, worshipped as the destroyer and transformer within the triad with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahma">Brahma</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vishnu">Vishnu</a>, and as the supreme being by Shaivas. He is depicted as an ascetic with a trident, the crescent moon and a third eye, as the cosmic dancer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nataraja">Nataraja</a>, and above all in the aniconic linga. His mount is the bull Nandi, and his worship spread across South and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southeast-asia">Southeast Asia</a>, from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/champa">Champa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shiva.jpg" alt="Shiva" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Indianhilbilly · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bangalore_Shiva.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
